for (i = 0; i < iter; i++) {
    __c = ror8(candiates, i);
    if ((__c & 0x1) == 0x1) {
        loc = i;
        goto out;
    }
}
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a new loop that checks for the first candidate clock sample value when no best value is found. This ensures that if there are candidate values available, the function will return the first usable candidate instead of returning `-EIO`, thus allowing the eMMC to operate correctly even when the best clock sample is not found.

